{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_en", "label": "README (English)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "readme_en_conductor", "label": "Conductor (discipline system for AI agents)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Makes any AI follow an engineering methodology \u2014 classify the task before starting, prove the result before claiming done and before every commit \u2014 and works only together with the global values file, which is a condition of operation rather than a recommendation."}, {"id": "readme_en_methodology", "label": "Methodology layer (core + playbooks + method dispatcher)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The nature of the task picks the approach (control group, instrumentation, jury of variants), so the dispatcher sits above the individual playbooks."}, {"id": "readme_en_proportional_verification", "label": "Proportional verification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verification follows the change, not the commit: a label edit needs only diff inspection, while behavior changes need affected checks, and applicable results can be reused."}, {"id": "readme_en_memory_layer", "label": "Memory layer (inbox + digested lessons)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two stores instead of one so every AI on the machine can append one line per lesson, while curated files plus an index stay searchable; recency is only a tie-breaker in relevance."}, {"id": "readme_en_lessons_inbox", "label": "Lessons inbox (~/.claude/conductor/lessons.md)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "readme_en_lessons_store", "label": "Digested lesson store (~/.claude/conductor/lessons/)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "readme_en_commit_discipline", "label": "Commit discipline (textual rule)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The marker git gate of earlier versions was removed because field data showed agents performed the evidence runs anyway, while the lock demanded an extra marker file that confirmed nothing and broke the commit when forgotten."}, {"id": "readme_en_evidence_store", "label": "Local verification evidence store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept outside the project and never uploaded because arguments and output can contain secrets; truncated or damaged evidence cannot justify reuse."}, {"id": "readme_en_reply_language", "label": "Reply language setting (~/.claude/conductor/reply-language)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rules are written entirely in English because the model reasons in the language of its instructions, and a Russian rule corpus dragged the visible reasoning into Russian even when another reply language was chosen; the language lives in a single substituted phrase that must not be hand-edited in the repository masters, otherwise --language stops switching anything."}, {"id": "readme_en_superpowers", "label": "superpowers (Claude Code plugin)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Installed rather than disabled as before, because Conductor is the process spine while superpowers supplies the skills on top of it."}, {"id": "readme_en_rtk", "label": "rtk (terminal output compressor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wiring is left to rtk's own `rtk init -g` rather than reimplemented by the installer."}, {"id": "readme_en_graphify", "label": "graphify (codebase knowledge graph tool)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "readme_en_conductor_cli", "label": "conductor CLI (status / update / rollback)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Updates fetch the official main into a temporary directory and back up before writing; a manually edited managed file stops the update instead of being force-overwritten, and later user edits block rollback instead of being erased."}, {"id": "install", "label": "install.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "install_global", "label": "install-global.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Overwrites ~/.gemini/AGENTS.md and ~/.codex/AGENTS.md but preserves prior text in a timestamped backup and warns loudly about it."}, {"id": "install_project", "label": "install-project.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Installs adapters into a specific project so the rules are versioned along with it, overriding only that project's language."}, {"id": "install_companions", "label": "install-companions.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every failure is loud but never aborts the Conductor install \u2014 a tool that cannot be installed prints SKIP or FAIL with a reason and the installation carries on."}, {"id": "uninstall", "label": "uninstall.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately never deletes the global CLAUDE.md, and does not remove the three companion tools because they are user-level and live their own life."}, {"id": "tools_doctor", "label": "tools/doctor.sh (install health check)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "tools_build_digests", "label": "tools/build-digests.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "tools_journal_report", "label": "tools/journal-report.sh (test-run journal reader)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "tools_restore_memory", "label": "tools/restore-memory.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never overwrites a non-empty destination, and restores a particular project's snapshot only on a separate explicit command."}, {"id": "tools_schedule_memory_backup", "label": "tools/schedule-memory-backup.ps1", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Offers a preview and never replaces an existing scheduled task."}, {"id": "qa_lint", "label": "qa/lint.sh (budget, wiring and wording linter)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "qa_lint_selftest", "label": "qa/lint-selftest.sh (negative lint self-test)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "qa_settings_json_test", "label": "qa/settings-json-test.py (config-edit tests)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "conductor_evidence_cli", "label": "conductor/evidence/cli.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`check` never executes: MATCH means observed conditions match, not a new passing test, so the agent must still inspect input coverage and output applicability."}, {"id": "memory_recall", "label": "memory/recall.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retrieves lexical candidates only and leaves meaning and applicability to the agent; read failures or exceeded budgets return PARTIAL rather than a successful empty result."}, {"id": "memory_recall_md", "label": "memory/recall.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "memory_migrate_lessons", "label": "memory/migrate-lessons.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shipped beside runtime so lesson maintenance works without a source checkout."}, {"id": "deploy_global_claude", "label": "deploy/global-CLAUDE.md (global values file)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mandatory because the baseline run without Conductor still passed all 13 discipline trials \u2014 the values file, not a bare model, produced that behavior; if the rules duplicating it were removed and the file deleted, discipline would vanish without a single error message."}, {"id": "runtime_playbooks_verification", "label": "runtime/playbooks/verification.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "playbooks_distill", "label": "playbooks/distill.md (lesson digestion)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_memory_recovery", "label": "docs/memory-recovery.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "adapters_core_body", "label": "adapters/core-body.md (shared rules text)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never edited by hand: the Cursor and Antigravity digests are built from it, because the repository is the source of truth and live copies are always rebuilt."}, {"id": "qa_reports_baseline", "label": "qa/reports/baseline.md (control-group results)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "qa_reports_baseline_values_file", "label": "qa/reports/baseline-values-file.md (starting conditions)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Records that the first measurement ran on a trimmed 56-line Russian copy of the values file, which bounds what the proof covers."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_report_v2", "label": "qa/reports/ab-report-v2.md (2026-08-15 A/B rerun)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Repeated the measurement on the shipped English file in full and on the current model generation: 27/27 traps in both arms at n=5, with the Conductor arm adding bug reproduction before the fix at a moderate +2 turn median cost."}, {"id": "github_workflows_ci", "label": ".github/workflows/ci.yml", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.en.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/Morqqulis/co